{
  "tema": 6145,
  "slug": "pronombres-verbo-conjugado",
  "titulo": "Position of pronouns with conjugated verbs",
  "subtitulo": "Lo compré, no lo toques, me lo recomendó.",
  "foto": "t01.jpg",
  "regla": "With a conjugated verb (any tense) and with negative commands, object and reflexive pronouns go in front of the verb, as separate words: lo compré, no lo toques. Order: reflexive, then indirect, then direct (se me, me lo).",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Direct object pronouns (**lo, la, los, las**...), indirect ones (**me, te, le, nos, les**) and reflexive ones (**me, te, se, nos**) all go **in front of a conjugated verb**, as separate words."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "(no) +",
            "pronoun(s)",
            "+ conjugated verb"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "That includes compound tenses: the pronoun goes before **haber**: **nos han mandado**, **se habían bañado**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Unlike English, the pronoun never goes after a conjugated verb: **los compré**, not ~~compré los~~."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: a conjugated verb is a wall; the pronouns line up in front of it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Ellos ==nos== han mandado una invitación.",
              "en": "They've sent us an invitation."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Me== lees un cuento esta noche?",
              "en": "Will you read me a story tonight?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Rosario ==lo== compró en la farmacia.",
              "en": "Rosario bought it at the pharmacy."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ellas ==se== habían bañado antes de salir.",
              "en": "They had showered before going out."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Los== compré en Guadalajara.",
              "en": "I bought them in Guadalajara."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "negativo",
      "titulo": "Negative commands",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With **negative commands**, the pronoun also goes in front, right after **no**:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "¡No ==me== dejes!",
              "en": "Don't leave me!"
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==lo== toques. Está muy caliente.",
              "en": "Don't touch it. It's very hot."
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==te== preocupes.",
              "en": "Don't worry."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "orden",
      "titulo": "More than one pronoun",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Order",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "indirect + direct",
              "**me lo**, **nos la**, **se lo** (le → se)"
            ],
            [
              "reflexive + indirect",
              "**se me**, **se te**, **se nos**"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Ella ==se lo== entregó enseguida.",
              "en": "She handed it to him right away. (se = to him, lo = it)"
            },
            {
              "es": "Me gusta este bar. Clara ==me lo== recomendó.",
              "en": "I like this bar. Clara recommended it to me."
            },
            {
              "es": "Antonio ==nos la== mandó desde Perú.",
              "en": "Antonio sent it to us from Peru."
            },
            {
              "es": "El susto ==se me== pasó pronto.",
              "en": "I got over the scare quickly. (se = reflexive, me = indirect)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Compré los ayer."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Los compré ayer."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Lo me dio."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Me lo dio."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Indirect before direct."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "No toques lo."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "No lo toques."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Negative command: in front."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Han nos llamado."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Nos han llamado."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "In front of **haber**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "parientes",
